// S441 reproducer — addendum-3 T1: a structural cell decl + function written directly in a `<db>` body
// (no `${ }`) silently drops the decl, the function AND every markup sibling after it.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/tut-db-body-decls-silently-dropped.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: a refusal. §34 E-STATE-BLOCK-STATEMENT-FORM row: "A state-block body is markup context, NOT a
//           `default-logic` locus (§4.18.1)"; S375 ruling 1 (recorded on g-state-block-statement-form-misses-a-
//           wrapped-statement): logic at a `<db>`/state-block locus is REFUSED. The siblings W-STATE-BLOCK-BARE-
//           WRITE-DECL (`@x = init`) and E-STATE-BLOCK-STATEMENT-FORM (`on mount`) exist for other forms.
// Actual:   exit 0, ZERO diagnostics. The HTML <body> holds only the two <script> tags; client.js contains no
//           reference to the cell or the function (grep count 0) — the button and paragraph are gone too.
//           Control: the same body with the cell + function wrapped in `${ }` → both emitted, 7 renders.
//           Variant: a `function …{}` line alone (no cell decl) is emitted into the page as literal TEXT.
<program db="t1.db">
<schema>
    notes { id: integer primary key
            body: text }
</>
<db src="t1.db" tables="notes">
    <count> = 7
    function bump() { @count = @count + 1 }
    <button onclick=bump()>go</button>
    <p>${@count}</p>
</db>
</program>
